# Explain implementation (cursor-packs)

**CONSTRAINT:** When the agent finishes an implementation or fix that changed project files, or when the user asks what changed / how it was built / what a finished run did, MUST Read and follow `.cursor/skills/explain-implementation/SKILL.md` before the final user-facing reply.

- MUST: short lead + numbered IF/ELSE steps that stay concrete (one clear action or decision per step; plain section headings OK; parenthetical why-it-matters on phase titles; small diagram MAY help).
- MUST: use present tense for how a change works; past tense for what already executed; keep parentheticals in the same tense (`no folds applied`, not `no folds to apply`).
- MUST: when a diagram shows loops, draw each loop as a subgraph with an in-loop retry edge; once-only steps (for example ledger RLM) sit outside those subgraphs.
- MUST NOT: pack write/push/open into one vague line.
- MUST NOT: label a lone box `Loop A` / `Loop B` on a straight-line flowchart (hides what is inside the loop).
- MUST NOT: end with only a file list / "want me to commit?" and no explain.
- MUST NOT: ship a prose essay for the explain pass.
- Enforcement: Before send on an implement/fix or post-run explain turn, confirm the skill was applied to the reply draft; if loops appear, confirm subgraph boundaries.
- Violation: STOP, Read the skill, rewrite the reply, then send.

CORRECT:
```text
Lead (+ optional headings) + numbered IF/ELSE steps with (why it matters); past if the run finished; optional mermaid with loop subgraphs
```

PROHIBITED:
```text
Multi-paragraph walkthrough, or "Done. Tests pass. Commit?", or Loop A → ledger → Loop B as three opaque boxes
```

Chat voice remains `.cursor/rules/always-rules-01-human-interaction.mdc` outside this explain pass. This rule requires a scannable step-by-step explain.
